                <pb facs="0233" n="140" xml:id="pg140"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.34119/170: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-09-14T17:00:00-04:00">September 14, 1935—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>205. From Dawson. Department’s telegram No. 110, July 25, 6 p.m. Learned this
                    morning from the chairman of the Bolivian and Paraguayan delegations that
                    Barreda Laos, senior Peruvian delegate, had submitted to them a proposal for the
                    setting up of a war responsibility tribunal which they were apparently disposed
                    to accept. Tribunal would be composed of three members, one each to be selected
                    by name by Bolivia and Paraguay, and the third to be a Justice of the Supreme
                    Court of the United States. Plan provides for first meeting of tribunal within 4
                    months of signature of agreement with 8 months for handing down of opinion.</p>
                <p>Barreda has not consulted or informed the neutrals including other members of the
                    committee set up to deal with the matter.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Rio de Janeiro. [Dawson.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
